# 2. REV Hardware Client Setup

## 2.1 Connect

1. Power motor with battery.
2. Connect USB-C from laptop to SPARK MAX.
3. Open REV Hardware Client.
4. Click **Scan for Devices**.

Verify:

☐ SPARK MAX found

☐ Firmware current

☐ Device reports NEO Brushless connected

☐ Encoder values visible

If the motor shows "Brushed" or encoder data is missing, stop and investigate.

---

## 2.2 Assign CAN ID

If this is a new controller:

Example:

☐ Elevator = CAN 20

Set:

☐ Device → CAN ID → 20

Apply settings.

☐ Label the controller physically.

---

## 2.3 Update Firmware

☐ Check firmware version.

If update available:

☐ Update Firmware

Reboot controller.

☐ Rescan.

☐ Verify controller reconnects successfully.

---

## 2.4 Factory Reset / LED Reference

For a brand-new motor or reused electronics:

☐ Set Factory Defaults

This eliminates mystery settings left from previous seasons.

### 2.4.1 Quick LED reference for a NEO:

🟦🟩 Cyan Blinking = GOOD Brushless motor configured, waiting for commands

🟦🟩 Cyan Solid = GOOD Brushless motor receiving commands

🟧🟨 Orange/Yellow = Check CAN wiring

🟧🟪 Orange/Magenta = Check encoder/sensor

🟧🟦 Orange/Blue = Controller has USB but no robot battery

⬜🟨 White/Yellow = Firmware update running

⚫ Off = No power, recovery mode, or corrupted firmware

### 2.4.2 Detailed LED reference for a NEO:
|LED Color / Pattern|Meaning|
|---|---|
|🟦🟩 Cyan Blinking|Brushless mode, Brake mode, no signal|
|🟦🟩 Cyan Solid|Brushless mode, Brake mode, valid signal|
|🟪 Magenta Blinking|Brushless mode, Coast mode, no signal|
|🟪 Magenta Solid|Brushless mode, Coast mode, valid signal|
|🟩 Green Blinking|Partial forward output|
|🟩 Green Solid|Full forward output|
|🟥 Red Blinking|Partial reverse output|
|🟥 Red Solid|Full reverse output|
|🟩⬜ Green/White Blinking|Forward limit switch active|
|🟥⬜ Red/White Blinking|Reverse limit switch active|
|⬜🟪 White/Magenta Fast Blink|Device Identify|
|⬜🟨 White/Yellow Blink|Firmware update in progress|
|⬜🟦 White/Blue Blink|Firmware update retry|
|🟧🟦 Orange/Blue Slow Blink|No 12V power (USB only)|
|🟧🟪 Orange/Magenta Slow Blink|Sensor fault|
|🟧🟦🟩 Orange/Cyan Slow Blink|Internal gate driver fault|
|🟧🟨 Orange/Yellow Slow Blink|CAN communication fault|
|⚫ Off|Recovery mode, corrupt firmware, or no power|
