# 3. Basic Configuration

On the SPARK MAX page:

## 3.1 Motor Type

Verify:

☐ Brushless

A NEO must be configured as brushless.

---

## 3.2 Idle Mode

Set:

☐ Brake

Reason:

An elevator should not free-fall when output goes to zero.

☐ Apply configuration.

---

## 3.3 Current Limit

Conservative starting point:

☐ 40A Smart Current Limit

For initial bring-up.

This helps protect mechanisms during setup mistakes.

---

## 3.4 Ramp Rate

Optional but recommended:

☐ 0.25 seconds

Prevents commands from shock-loading the elevator.

---

# 4. Encoder Verification

Without commanding motion:

☐ Observe encoder display.

☐ Manually move elevator a few inches.

Verify:

☐ Position changes

☐ Velocity changes

☐ Record the current reading.

Example:

Position = 5.37 rotations

If values don't change:

☐ Check motor connection

☐ Check controller status

☐ Reboot SPARK MAX

Do not continue until encoder works.

---

# 5. First Motor Motion

Open:

☐ Control Tab

Select:

☐ Duty Cycle Mode

Set output:

☐ 2%

☐ Click run.

Observe:

- Motor direction
- Gearbox
- Elevator movement

Stop immediately if:

- Binding occurs
- Chain jumps
- Current spikes
- Unusual sounds appear

---

# 6. Establish Elevator Direction

Run:

☐ +5%

Desired result:

☐ Elevator Up

If it goes down:

Use:

☐ Invert Motor inside Hardware Client.

☐ Retest.

Standardize on:

☐ Positive = Up

This simplifies future code and PID tuning.

---

# 7. Measure Elevator Travel

Keep speed between:

5% and 10%

☐ Slowly jog upward.

Record:

## 7.1 Bottom

☐ Position = 0.00

(or whatever reading exists)

## 7.2 Top

Example:

Position = 82.4 rotations

☐ Record this in your engineering notebook in GitHub.

Future software limit:

82.4 rotations

---

# 8. Current Monitoring

While jogging:

Watch:

☐ Motor Current

☐ Bus Voltage

☐ Temperature

Typical observations:

|Condition|Current|
|---|---|
|Free movement|5-15A|
|Moderate load|15-30A|
|Binding|40A+|

If current suddenly jumps:

☐ STOP

Find the mechanical issue first.

---

# 9. Verify Brake Mode

Move elevator upward.

Command:

☐ 0%

☐ Observe.

Expected:

☐ Elevator remains nearly stationary

If it rapidly drops:

- Verify Brake Mode applied
- Check if the elevator is heavily overhung
- Consider future feedforward/counterbalance

